*** Resetting replication at the very beginning of the test.

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Initializing the @checkpoints session variable (a JSON array) for
*** storing (binlog name, position) checkpoints.

*** Saving the ["":4] checkpoint (everything from the beginning of the
*** oldest binary log file).

*** Step 0: Saving the initial binary log position.

*** Step 1: Creating tbl.
CREATE TABLE tbl(
id INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
value VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,
PRIMARY KEY(id)
) ENGINE=InnoDB;

*** Step 2: Inserting the first batch of rows.
INSERT INTO tbl VALUES (1, 'one'), (2, 'two'), (3, 'three');

*** Step 3: Flushing the source binary log for the first time.
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Step 4: Inserting the second batch of rows.
INSERT INTO tbl VALUES (4, 'four'), (5, 'five'), (6, 'six');

*** Step 5: Flushing the source binary log for the second time.
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Step 6: Flushing the source binary log for the third time (producing an
*** empty binary log file).
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Step 7: Inserting the third batch of rows.
INSERT INTO tbl VALUES (7, 'seven'), (8, 'eight'), (9, 'nine');

*** Saving end-of-file positions (sizes) of all binary log files as
*** checkpoints.
include/assert.inc [There must be exactly 4 binary log files]

*** Fetching the source binary logs in position mode.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode.
include/read_file_to_var.inc

*** Waiting for the replication source listener port ready to accept
*** connections.

